{"id":"000VOT","title":"Dutch Masyu","author":"yttrio","solvedCount":2,"difficulty":3,"rating":"N/A","firstSeen":"2026-10-23T22:17:30+00:00","posted":"Gestern, 23:31 Uhr","rules":"This is my second Masyu/Sudoku hybrid, the first of which was Modular Masyu, which contains an example image to clarify how the digits in circle clues work.\n\nRules:\n\nNormal Sudoku rules apply.\n\nMasyu: Draw a single non-intersecting loop through the centers of some cells that passes through every circle clue. The loop must turn on black circles and pass straight through the cells on either side. The loop must go straight through white circles and turn in at least one of the cells on either side.\n\nThe loop acts as a Dutch Whispers line (i.e., adjacent digits on the loop must have a difference of at least 4).\n\nThe digit in each given circle clue counts the total number of loop cells in all straight loop segments coming of of the cell (counting the cells where the loop turns, and counting the clued cell itself once).\n\nSudokuPad","solutionCode":"Digits on the loop in row 2 (left to right) followed by digits on the loop in row 8 (left to right)","tags":["Sudoku","Masyu"],"links":[{"url":"https://sudokupad.app/6tx9igk01f","kind":"sudokupad"}],"data":"","error":null,"settings":{},"link":"https://sudokupad.app/6tx9igk01f","linkKind":"sudokupad","summary":{"format":"scl","decoded":true,"rows":9,"cols":9,"cages":0,"hasSolution":true,"features":["underlays"]},"attempts":0,"fetched":"2026-10-23T22:17:30+00:00"}